<button class="markup-toc-button">Show Table of Contents</button></div>Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Subtlety Rogue DPS in Cataclysm Classic Phase 4. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Dragon Soul, Firelands, Twilight Protocol Dungeons, and Valor Points. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c4"> Best in Slot Gear for Subtlety Rogue DPS Phase 4</span></h2>A Subtlety Rogue's first priorities are meeting the expertise and hit caps of 6.5% and 8% respectively. Expertise will be a bit tricky depending on what gear you already have to work with. Hit, on the other hand, is made very easy to do thanks to our talent <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=13843/precision">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_marksmanship.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precision</span></a>. Due to the low value that mastery and crit have, you will usually find yourself reforging to hit if you are already at expertise cap and the item already has haste on it. Once you hit the spell hit cap, the value of hit completely drops and you'll be better off picking up crit.<br/>
<br/>With the introduction of the reforging system, we will be able to take 40% of an unwanted or lesser valued stat and switch it over to a secondary stat that is not already present on the piece. As a  general rule, you'll aim to get your expertise cap and then make sure every piece has haste and crit on it ideally by reforging off mastery and hit.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit Rating - As mentioned, you will need to reach your hit cap of 8% (2% after <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=13843/precision">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_marksmanship.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precision</span></a>). This should be automatically met with excess with any decent set of gear. If you find yourself below this benchmark, simply look to reforge an item to hit.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise Rating - Expertise reduces the chance for our attacks to be dodged or parried. We will always want to hit this cap of 6.5% or 781 rating to ensure we're never missing any special attacks or autos.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Agility - Agility is the primary base stat for rogues, and is always good to get more of. We passively get 5% more of this stat in Cataclysm thanks to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86531/leather-specialization">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leather Specialization</span></a> and an extra 30% thanks to subtlety's <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=31220/sinister-calling">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_sinistercalling.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sinister Calling</span></a>. Agility gives 2 attack power per point and a little bit of critical strike chance for your attacks.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - This stat directly increases our energy regeneration in Cataclys m which is a big change for both the <a class="icontiny c4" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=4/rogue">
<img alt="Rogue" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_rogue.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rogue</span></a> and <a class="icontiny c11" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=11/druid">
<img alt="Druid" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Druid</span></a>. Haste is a very valuable stat for subtlety because it also increases our attack speed and helps smooth out our rotation.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - This has the same effect it has always had in that it increases our critical strike chance doubling the amount of damage done when we do crit. Unlike the other rogue specializations, subtlety doesn't mind having crit on their gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - Mastery is an all new stat introduced in Cataclysm that has a unique effect based on whatever specialization you are playing. For Subtlety, the mastery is <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=76808/executioner">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Executioner</span></a>. This directly increases the damage of our finishers as well as the effectiveness of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=5171/slice-and-dice">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_slicedice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Slice and Dice</span></a>.</div></li></ol>
